1
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:37,704
<i>We really need Chiara's help.</i>

2
00:00:37,787 --> 00:00:40,331
We need to bring down La Morte Bianca.

3
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:50,675
We need support from her active followers

4
00:00:50,759 --> 00:00:54,095
so La Morte Bianca won't suspect us.

5
00:00:54,179 --> 00:00:56,264
Understood? Sir?

6
00:00:58,224 --> 00:00:59,642
Once all of this is over,

7
00:00:59,726 --> 00:01:01,519
I hope we can be friends.

8
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:04,397
Just like we were at the bar,
when we first met.

9
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:14,532
If there is something wrong at the island,

10
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:16,993
why are they the only ones affected?

11
00:01:17,077 --> 00:01:20,205
They brought something home
that shouldn't be there,

12
00:01:20,288 --> 00:01:25,043
so you all should stay away
from their house.

13
00:01:25,126 --> 00:01:27,670
Those who go there also get sick.

14
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:31,883
but it's not my birthday.

15
00:01:31,966 --> 00:01:32,842
But still, thanks a lot.

16
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:57,075
Sorry about that, Agent Alex.

17
00:01:57,826 --> 00:02:01,079
We threw you a surprise party,
and it wasn't even your birthday.

18
00:02:01,955 --> 00:02:04,040
It was all Sianong's fault.

19
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:07,669
He kept reminding us about your birthday.

20
00:02:07,752 --> 00:02:10,046
He even gave us an hourly countdown!

21
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:12,132
And it turned out he got it wrong!

22
00:02:12,215 --> 00:02:14,592
I really think
he's mathematically challenged.

23
00:02:15,677 --> 00:02:18,429
Hey, don't underestimate
Sianong's math skills.

24
00:02:18,513 --> 00:02:21,099
He can calculate exactly how many bullets
will hit your body

25
00:02:21,182 --> 00:02:22,475
if he hears you say that.

26
00:02:26,938 --> 00:02:30,567
Then why did his math skills fail
when it came to your birthday?

27
00:02:32,777 --> 00:02:34,362
I think I know why.

28
00:02:35,572 --> 00:02:36,739
I told him

29
00:02:37,323 --> 00:02:39,450
that my father's birthday is next week.

30
00:02:39,534 --> 00:02:43,079
So maybe the only part he heard
was "next week."

31
00:02:47,041 --> 00:02:48,877
Well then, happy birthday to your dad!

32
00:03:01,389 --> 00:03:02,765
That's why

33
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:06,144
I haven't celebrated
my birthday in a long time.

34
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:10,273
You know,

35
00:03:12,817 --> 00:03:14,777
all this time, I felt like

36
00:03:15,987 --> 00:03:19,574
my father chose to serve the country
instead of being with me.

37
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,705
But on the other hand,

38
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:28,958
it feels like

39
00:03:31,002 --> 00:03:33,504
he also gave his life for me,

40
00:03:33,588 --> 00:03:35,590
to protect my future.

41
00:03:37,967 --> 00:03:40,011
That's just how fathers are.

42
00:03:42,096 --> 00:03:44,140
On the outside, they act so tough,

43
00:03:44,974 --> 00:03:46,768
but on the inside,

44
00:03:48,144 --> 00:03:49,896
if you really look into their hearts,

45
00:03:51,397 --> 00:03:54,609
they always make
the biggest space for their children.

46
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:56,903
You know,

47
00:03:57,737 --> 00:04:02,116
I'm absolutely sure
your father is so proud of you.

48
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:13,002
Your father was a hero.

49
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:22,053
Can't someone be a hero

50
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:26,349
without having to die
and leaving loved ones behind?

51
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:35,525
I didn't mean
to romanticize your father's death.

52
00:04:42,699 --> 00:04:44,784
People only remember the hero.

53
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:47,328
But the truth is,

54
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:49,956
he died while on duty.

55
00:04:51,582 --> 00:04:53,126
He trusted too much.

56
00:04:55,211 --> 00:04:56,379
What do you mean?

57
00:04:57,422 --> 00:04:58,715
Someone betrayed him?

58
00:05:01,634 --> 00:05:02,885
Something like that.

59
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:07,432
Someone he considered
a friend in the agency

60
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:11,269
turned out to be a double agent.

61
00:05:13,479 --> 00:05:15,023
Working for the enemy.

62
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:20,320
So, my dad became collateral damage.

63
00:05:23,197 --> 00:05:26,701
But of course,
the agency found out too late.

64
00:05:28,036 --> 00:05:29,662
The investigation took a long time.

65
00:05:31,873 --> 00:05:32,957
But

66
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:35,335
it's amazing, though.

67
00:05:36,252 --> 00:05:37,920
After everything that happened to him,

68
00:05:38,713 --> 00:05:41,174
you still had the courage
to join the service.

69
00:05:42,508 --> 00:05:44,052
You're really something, you know?

70
00:05:48,848 --> 00:05:50,141
That's why I'm guarded.

71
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:53,603
It's hard for me to trust.

72
00:05:56,481 --> 00:05:58,941
Trust isn't something simple, Mikoy.

73
00:06:00,651 --> 00:06:02,528
Especially in this line of work.

74
00:06:07,992 --> 00:06:09,535
So you be careful too.

75
00:06:14,499 --> 00:06:15,583
Thank you.

76
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:23,591
What about Chiara?

77
00:06:24,342 --> 00:06:25,968
Do you still doubt her?

78
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:34,143
I'll be honest with you, Mikoy.

79
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,315
I trust you, Mikoy.

80
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:43,986
But not Chiara.

81
00:07:10,304 --> 00:07:11,389
Angelito!

82
00:07:13,766 --> 00:07:14,767
What happened to you?

83
00:07:21,941 --> 00:07:23,192
Are you okay?

84
00:07:23,276 --> 00:07:24,360
What happened?

85
00:07:32,785 --> 00:07:34,245
Are you feeling better?

86
00:07:34,328 --> 00:07:36,497
I'm okay. It's probably
just an upset stomach.

87
00:07:37,081 --> 00:07:37,915
Just look at you.

88
00:07:37,999 --> 00:07:41,627
Angelito, Aunt Gina said
you've been throwing up.

89
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:43,212
Do you want to go to the hospital?

90
00:07:44,172 --> 00:07:46,174
No. I'll be fine.

91
00:07:46,257 --> 00:07:48,217
I'll feel better
once I take some medicine.

92
00:07:57,727 --> 00:08:00,605
All right. You said you're okay,
but if you're not,

93
00:08:00,688 --> 00:08:01,898
just let me know.

94
00:08:01,981 --> 00:08:03,649
Before it gets any worse.

95
00:08:20,666 --> 00:08:23,794
Yes. I wonder what happened
at the Concordat.

96
00:08:24,670 --> 00:08:28,341
Then again, she's the head,
so it doesn't matter what they decided.

97
00:08:28,424 --> 00:08:31,135
Why don't we ask her why she's so happy?

98
00:08:57,119 --> 00:08:59,872
She only has three islands left to search.

99
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:01,916
We're running out of time. What do we do?

100
00:09:10,258 --> 00:09:13,135
We don't even have a pigeon
to deliver a secret message

101
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:14,679
to our daughter.

102
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:19,058
How?

103
00:09:44,458 --> 00:09:45,668
Hurry!

104
00:09:52,550 --> 00:09:54,594
Be careful with your plan, darling.

105
00:09:54,677 --> 00:09:57,888
You might end up digging your own grave.

106
00:09:57,972 --> 00:10:00,600
La Morte Bianca will surely catch on.

107
00:10:39,221 --> 00:10:41,390
La Morte Bianca.

108
00:10:59,075 --> 00:11:00,076
Is this okay?

109
00:11:00,159 --> 00:11:01,410
Won't Ma'am Isabella get mad?

110
00:11:01,994 --> 00:11:03,829
The rider said it's for Ma'am Donabel.

111
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:06,999
For me? That's my package?

112
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:08,084
Give it to me.

113
00:11:09,794 --> 00:11:11,253
Is it yours? What's inside?

114
00:11:12,296 --> 00:11:14,632
Well, it's for beauty.

115
00:11:16,967 --> 00:11:20,888
At this point, only chickens
live a stress-free life.

116
00:11:21,889 --> 00:11:24,642
If it works, I'll give you some, okay?

117
00:11:25,559 --> 00:11:26,977
- Okay?
- Okay, ma'am.

118
00:11:30,439 --> 00:11:32,566
You're acting like a mother.

119
00:11:34,026 --> 00:11:36,946
A mother? Can't I just be
his girl best friend?

120
00:11:39,323 --> 00:11:42,159
- You really are something.
- By the way, where's Laurence?

121
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:46,038
He went with Aunt Gina to get some ginger.

122
00:11:46,122 --> 00:11:49,083
You know ginger tea is the best remedy
for an upset stomach.

123
00:11:58,926 --> 00:12:00,219
Hey, are you okay?

124
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:01,720
Do you still have a fever?

125
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:05,099
It's just a slight fever.

126
00:12:05,182 --> 00:12:06,183
A tiny one.

127
00:12:07,184 --> 00:12:08,394
A tiny fever.

128
00:12:10,729 --> 00:12:15,192
Maybe your body just got exhausted
from yesterday's activities.

129
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:17,945
- Maybe.
- Exhausted?

130
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:20,948
He wasn't even there yesterday.
He was helping someone.

131
00:12:21,824 --> 00:12:24,076
- That's it!
- Maybe you caught something

132
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:26,495
from the sick woman
you were helping, right?

133
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:28,956
You know, maybe you're right.

134
00:12:29,039 --> 00:12:31,750
Angelito, maybe you got infected there?

135
00:12:38,007 --> 00:12:40,176
This one's for me.

136
00:12:40,259 --> 00:12:41,927
There's no name on it,

137
00:12:42,011 --> 00:12:43,804
and there's no sender's address either.

138
00:12:45,514 --> 00:12:46,974
From Chiara?

139
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:54,565
Why would our daughter send us

140
00:12:54,648 --> 00:12:57,067
a blank piece of paper?

141
00:12:57,151 --> 00:12:58,819
What is this?

142
00:13:26,722 --> 00:13:30,684
- Leave this to me.
- All right, go ahead.

143
00:13:53,749 --> 00:13:55,167
Los Bandidos!

144
00:15:14,496 --> 00:15:15,539
He's alive!

145
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:27,968
Excuse me, <i>señora</i>.

146
00:15:28,552 --> 00:15:29,970
Yes.

147
00:16:20,646 --> 00:16:21,772
Dad?

148
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:37,871
Wait? Why?

149
00:16:38,914 --> 00:16:39,999
Where are you going?

150
00:16:40,499 --> 00:16:42,543
Can you stay here for a while?

151
00:16:43,919 --> 00:16:45,129
Just for a little while.

152
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:48,799
Please.

153
00:16:49,508 --> 00:16:51,552
I'm scared, Dad.

154
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:55,389
I don't know if…

155
00:16:57,433 --> 00:16:59,560
if I'm still doing the right thing.

156
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:05,566
It's so hard to choose what's right.

157
00:17:07,317 --> 00:17:08,902
There are so many complications.

158
00:17:13,365 --> 00:17:17,870
You used to say
that as long as it's done out of love,

159
00:17:20,205 --> 00:17:22,207
you can overcome any fear.

160
00:17:27,713 --> 00:17:32,134
But why is it that now that I've learned
to love and trust again,

161
00:17:34,803 --> 00:17:37,473
everything feels even harder?

162
00:17:41,518 --> 00:17:42,644
Dad!

163
00:17:43,854 --> 00:17:44,980
Dad!

164
00:17:46,815 --> 00:17:47,900
Dad!

165
00:18:31,527 --> 00:18:34,530
Before you start overthinking,

166
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:36,949
let me answer the questions
running through your mind.

167
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:44,123
Yes, I'm having trouble sleeping too, and…

168
00:18:44,873 --> 00:18:47,668
no, I'm not going to kill you.

169
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:54,007
At least I don't have to waste my breath
asking questions anymore.

170
00:18:58,720 --> 00:18:59,847
I heard

171
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:02,891
you were calling out to your father.

172
00:19:05,894 --> 00:19:07,688
Did you dream about him?

173
00:19:12,901 --> 00:19:14,695
Whatever you heard, it was nothing.

174
00:19:27,708 --> 00:19:29,001
Because I do.

175
00:19:35,215 --> 00:19:37,176
But honestly,

176
00:19:38,677 --> 00:19:43,056
I hated how controlling he was
when I was growing up.

177
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:46,560
We argued about it all the time.

178
00:19:47,769 --> 00:19:49,146
But now…

179
00:19:50,689 --> 00:19:52,399
I miss it.

180
00:19:54,818 --> 00:19:56,069
Isn't that weird?

181
00:19:57,237 --> 00:19:58,947
When they're still around,

182
00:20:00,908 --> 00:20:02,868
we take them for granted.

183
00:20:03,827 --> 00:20:06,580
But once they're gone,

184
00:20:07,581 --> 00:20:09,708
that's when we realize

185
00:20:10,292 --> 00:20:13,962
how much we really needed them.

186
00:20:17,424 --> 00:20:19,927
Turns out we never really hated them.

187
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:29,353
You know, you're lucky.
Your dad's still with you.

188
00:20:31,146 --> 00:20:33,273
You still have a chance to be with him.

189
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:45,827
But you're right.

190
00:20:58,674 --> 00:21:02,052
I just hope this fight ends soon.

191
00:21:03,387 --> 00:21:05,555
So you can visit your father.

192
00:21:07,307 --> 00:21:10,519
And I can finally be with my family again.

193
00:21:54,521 --> 00:21:55,689
Séance.

194
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:13,582
She hasn't appeared to us.

195
00:23:34,162 --> 00:23:35,914
So I'm Ko-ryan.

196
00:24:19,332 --> 00:24:22,002
We have a bigger problem now.

197
00:24:22,085 --> 00:24:24,629
<i>Quintin knows about the bomb.</i>

198
00:24:25,213 --> 00:24:26,798
That's not impossible to happen.

199
00:24:36,641 --> 00:24:37,642
<i>Sofie called.</i>

200
00:24:38,351 --> 00:24:39,436
<i>Angelito is sick.</i>

201
00:24:43,982 --> 00:24:46,193
Any news about Angelito?

202
00:24:46,276 --> 00:24:47,944
Mikoy, Angelito is sick.
